<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jānis Čakste</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1859">1859</a>–<a href="/years/1927">1927</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jānis Čakste was a Latvian lawyer and statesman who was the first president of Latvia, serving from 1922 until his death in 1927. A member of the Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-duma">State Duma</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, he chaired the People's Council that proclaimed Latvian independence in November 1918 and then the Constitutional Assembly that adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-latvia">Satversme</a> of 1922.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janis-cakste.jpg" alt="Jānis Čakste" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ei tiedossa · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Janis_Cakste.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
